  "query_preview": "..\n(Today through Saturday)\n\nWEATHER PATTERN OVERVIEW: Warm and dry conditions are expected to \npersist through the remainder of the holiday weekend. Atmospheric \nmoisture will increase this afternoon, driven by low level southerly \nwinds. When combined with daytime heating and instability, the \nresult is isolated showers and thunderstorms in Humboldt County. \nThere is a very low chance for an isolated cell or two across the \nrest of the forecast area, but instability is much less favorable. \nAfternoon convective potential continues for Monday and Tuesday, \neven as building high pressure over the four corners area \nstrengthens. Ridging over Nevada and keeps temperatures unseasonably \nwarm, with high temperatures in the 90s. Convective potential \ndisappears by Wednesday as the high and ridge strengthen further, \nallowing temperatures to warm through the end of the week. High \ntemperatures will increase into the upper 90s, with a few areas even \nreaching triple digits by Friday and Saturday. Low temperatures are \nexpected to be in the 50s and low 60s. There is already a moderate \nlevel of HeatRisk for Friday afternoon and Saturday afternoon. These \ndays will need to be monitored for excessive heat impacts.\n\nFORECAST CONFIDENCE & DEVIATIONS: High confidence in above normal\ntemperatures through the forecast period, with moderate confidence\nin an additional warmup late week. Low confidence in showers and \nthunderstorms today through Tuesday. Moderate confidence in dry \nweather Wednesday and beyond.",
